        "original_id": "0e587686-57d9-551c-abdc-7b19ff392d50",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paola Suárez, Virginia Ruano Pascual, Michael Venus, Chan Hao-ching, Monica Niculescu\n- Sports: Tennis, doubles, singles, Grand Slam titles, rankings\n\nFacts:\n- Paola Suárez was born on 23 June 1976 and is a retired professional tennis player from Argentina.\n- Michael Venus reached a career-high singles ranking of No. 274 in July 2011.\n- Paola Suárez was one of the most prominent women's doubles players in the early and mid-2000s.\n- Paola Suárez won eight Grand Slam titles in women's doubles, and all eight titles were won with Virginia Ruano Pascual.\n- Paola Suárez held the No. 1 doubles ranking for 87 non-consecutive weeks.\n- Michael Venus is better known as a leading doubles player with a huge serve.\n- In 2017, Chan Hao-ching reached the Wimbledon women's doubles with Monica Niculescu and the US Open mixed doubles with Michael Venus.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
