        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8f592b8a-6b5e-5ddb-933f-6bbb60015dd4",
        "text": "Page: Paola Suárez. Sentence: Paola Suárez (born 23 June 1976) is a retired professional tennis player from Argentina.\nPage: Paola Suárez. Sentence: She was one of the most prominent women's doubles players throughout the early and mid-2000s, winning eight Grand Slam titles, all of them with Virginia Ruano Pascual, and holding the No. 1 doubles ranking for 87 non-consecutive weeks.\nPage: Michael Venus (tennis). Sentence: He reached a career high singles ranking of 274 in July 2011, but is much better known as a leading doubles player with a huge serve.\nPage: Chan Hao-ching. Sentence: She reached two more in 2017: the women's doubles at Wimbledon with Monica Niculescu, and the US Open mixed doubles with Michael Venus.",
